"use strict";(self.webpackChunkstrata_storage_docs=self.webpackChunkstrata_storage_docs||[]).push([["6607"],{7735(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"strata-storage-3-1-3","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-3","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-31-strata-storage-3.1.3.md","title":"Strata Storage 3.1.3","description":"Documentation only: the README drops its CI badge, because releases are built and verified locally.","date":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release","description":"Strata Storage releases, newest first."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"strata-storage-3-1-3","title":"Strata Storage 3.1.3","description":"Documentation only: the README drops its CI badge, because releases are built and verified locally.","date":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"lastUpdatedAt":1793427924000,"nextItem":{"title":"Strata Storage 3.1.4","permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-4"}},"content":"Documentation only: the README drops its CI badge, because releases are built and verified locally.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nDocumentation only: no code, API or `dist/` change.\\n\\n## Changed\\n\\n- **README:** the CI badge is gone (releases are built and verified locally; there is no hosted CI), and the\\n  Limitations section says the gates run before every release.\\n\\nFull history: [the changelog](/reference/changelog). Install: `yarn add strata-storage@3.1.3`."},{"id":"strata-storage-3-1-4","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-4","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-31-strata-storage-3.1.4.md","title":"Strata Storage 3.1.4","description":"The optional Firebase adapter names are now in StorageType; runtime behaviour is unchanged.","date":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release","description":"Strata Storage releases, newest first."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"strata-storage-3-1-4","title":"Strata Storage 3.1.4","description":"The optional Firebase adapter names are now in StorageType; runtime behaviour is unchanged.","date":"2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"lastUpdatedAt":1793628081000,"prevItem":{"title":"Strata Storage 3.1.3","permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-3"},"nextItem":{"title":"Strata Storage 3.1.2","permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-2"}},"content":"Version 3.1.4 fixes the TypeScript names for the optional Firebase adapters. After registering the Firestore or Realtime Database adapter, you can select `{ storage: \'firestore\' }` or `{ storage: \'realtime\' }` without a type cast.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nThe adapters already worked at runtime. This release adds their names to `StorageType` and updates the README\'s release guidance; it does not change runtime behaviour. Register the optional Firebase adapter before selecting it, and test the path your app uses.\\n\\nUpgrade with:\\n\\n```bash\\nyarn add strata-storage@3.1.4\\n```\\n\\nRead the [full changelog](/reference/changelog) for the exact release record."},{"id":"strata-storage-3-1-2","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-2","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-30-strata-storage-3.1.2.md","title":"Strata Storage 3.1.2","description":"No API change: the install script is gone, the CLI moved to bin/, and Android SDK fallbacks are 36.","date":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release","description":"Strata Storage releases, newest first."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"strata-storage-3-1-2","title":"Strata Storage 3.1.2","description":"No API change: the install script is gone, the CLI moved to bin/, and Android SDK fallbacks are 36.","date":"2026-10-30T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"lastUpdatedAt":1793384723000,"prevItem":{"title":"Strata Storage 3.1.4","permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-4"},"nextItem":{"title":"Strata Storage 3.1.1","permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-1"}},"content":"No API change: the install script is gone, the CLI moved to bin/, and Android SDK fallbacks are 36.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nNo JavaScript or API change: `dist/` is equivalent to 3.1.1\'s.\\n\\n## Removed\\n\\n- **The `postinstall` script.** Installing the package no longer runs anything in your project; the setup\\n  steps it printed (including `npx cap sync` for Capacitor apps) are in the README\'s Quick Start.\\n\\n## Changed\\n\\n- **The `npx strata-storage` CLI moved from `scripts/` to `bin/`.** The command is unchanged.\\n- **Android:** the fallback `compileSdkVersion` and `targetSdkVersion` (used only when your app does not set\\n  them) are now 36. Your app\'s own values still win.\\n- **Build and gates:** `tsc` + `tsc-alias` replace the custom build script, and `yarn gates` runs typecheck,\\n  lint, build and a Vitest suite against the built `dist/` (the storage-ownership predicate and the README\\n  version row).\\n\\nFull history: [the changelog](/reference/changelog). Install: `yarn add strata-storage@3.1.2`."},{"id":"strata-storage-3-1-1","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-1","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-21-strata-storage-3.1.1.md","title":"Strata Storage 3.1.1","description":"Same-key raw imports keep the migrated value (ISSUE-14).","date":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release","description":"Strata Storage releases, newest first."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"strata-storage-3-1-1","title":"Strata Storage 3.1.1","description":"Same-key raw imports keep the migrated value (ISSUE-14).","date":"2026-10-21T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"lastUpdatedAt":1793383927000,"prevItem":{"title":"Strata Storage 3.1.2","permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-2"},"nextItem":{"title":"Strata Storage 3.0.1","permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-0-1"}},"content":"Same-key raw imports keep the migrated value (ISSUE-14).\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Fixed\\n\\n- **Same-key raw imports preserve the migrated value** (ISSUE-14). When `keyPrefix: false` makes the named raw source and destination the same physical key, `importRawSync` now keeps the newly written Strata envelope instead of deleting it. Distinct-key imports still remove the source only after the destination write succeeds.\\n\\nFull history: [the changelog](/reference/changelog). Install: `yarn add strata-storage@3.1.1`."},{"id":"strata-storage-3-0-1","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-0-1","source":"@site/blog/2026-09-24-strata-storage-3.0.1.md","title":"Strata Storage 3.0.1","description":"Android: consuming apps on current AGP configure strata-storage again (ISSUE-12).","date":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release","description":"Strata Storage releases, newest first."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"strata-storage-3-0-1","title":"Strata Storage 3.0.1","description":"Android: consuming apps on current AGP configure strata-storage again (ISSUE-12).","date":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"lastUpdatedAt":1793383927000,"prevItem":{"title":"Strata Storage 3.1.1","permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-1"},"nextItem":{"title":"Strata Storage 3.1.0","permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-0"}},"content":"Android: consuming apps on current AGP configure strata-storage again (ISSUE-12).\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Fixed\\n\\n- **Android: consuming apps on current AGP failed to configure `:strata-storage`** (ISSUE-12).\\n  `android/build.gradle` referenced `getDefaultProguardFile(\'proguard-android.txt\')`, which current Android\\n  Gradle Plugin versions reject at configuration time because it includes `-dontoptimize` \u2014 so the whole\\n  app build failed even though the library sets `minifyEnabled false`. Now uses\\n  `proguard-android-optimize.txt`, like every official Capacitor plugin. No JavaScript or API change.\\n\\nFull history: [the changelog](/reference/changelog). Install: `yarn add strata-storage@3.0.1`."},{"id":"strata-storage-3-1-0","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-0","source":"@site/blog/2026-09-24-strata-storage-3.1.0.md","title":"Strata Storage 3.1.0","description":"importRawSync adopts one foreign localStorage or sessionStorage entry; sessionStorage keys are prefixed again (ISSUE-13).","date":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release","description":"Strata Storage releases, newest first."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"strata-storage-3-1-0","title":"Strata Storage 3.1.0","description":"importRawSync adopts one foreign localStorage or sessionStorage entry; sessionStorage keys are prefixed again (ISSUE-13).","date":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"lastUpdatedAt":1793383927000,"prevItem":{"title":"Strata Storage 3.0.1","permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-0-1"},"nextItem":{"title":"Strata Storage 3.0.0","permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-0-0"}},"content":"importRawSync adopts one foreign localStorage or sessionStorage entry; sessionStorage keys are prefixed again (ISSUE-13).\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Added\\n\\n- **`importRawSync(rawKey, key, options)`** \u2014 adopt ONE foreign `localStorage` / `sessionStorage` entry,\\n  named by its exact physical key, into a strata key, deleting the original. The migration path for data\\n  written by something other than this library (a pre-strata zustand store, a raw `setItem`), which the\\n  implicit paths deliberately never adopt. The raw string is kept as-is; an existing value at `key` wins and\\n  nothing is moved. Found while moving ZTools\' 22 zustand stores onto strata.\\n\\n## Fixed\\n\\n- **`sessionStorage` keys were not prefixed** (ISSUE-13). 3.0.0 documented both web areas as written under\\n  `strata:`, but `SessionStorageAdapter`\'s constructor defaulted its prefix to `\'\'`, overriding the shared\\n  default. It now uses `DEFAULT_WEB_KEY_PREFIX`; existing bare envelope keys migrate themselves on read.\\n\\nFull history: [the changelog](/reference/changelog). Install: `yarn add strata-storage@3.1.0`."},{"id":"strata-storage-3-0-0","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-0-0","source":"@site/blog/2026-09-01-strata-storage-3.0.0.md","title":"Strata Storage 3.0.0","description":"The web adapters now prefix their keys with strata:, with automatic migration of existing data.","date":"2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release","description":"Strata Storage releases, newest first."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"strata-storage-3-0-0","title":"Strata Storage 3.0.0","description":"The web adapters now prefix their keys with strata:, with automatic migration of existing data.","date":"2026-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"lastUpdatedAt":1793383927000,"prevItem":{"title":"Strata Storage 3.1.0","permalink":"/blog/strata-storage-3-1-0"}},"content":"The web adapters now prefix their keys with strata:, with automatic migration of existing data.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n**Breaking: the web adapters now prefix their keys with `strata:`.** One line restores the old behaviour,\\nand existing data migrates itself on read \u2014 but read the migration notes before upgrading, because a\\nconsumer that reads a physical key from outside this library must opt out.\\n\\n## Breaking\\n\\n- **`localStorage` and `sessionStorage` keys are now written under `strata:`.** `DEFAULT_WEB_KEY_PREFIX`\\n  is exported. Before this release the default prefix was the empty string, so this library\'s keys sat\\n  unprefixed among every other script\'s on the origin. 2.9.0 made that *safe* \u2014 a key is ours only if its\\n  value is a `StorageValue` envelope \u2014 and this makes it *tidy*, so our keys are identifiable by name too.\\n  - `cookies` are unchanged: they already defaulted to `strata_`, and moving them would break existing\\n    cookies for no gain.\\n  - `indexedDB` and `cache` own a named store, `memory` owns its own Map, and the URL adapter already\\n    prefixes its params. None of them can collide with another script\'s keys, so none of them change.\\n  - `namespace` is a separate mechanism and is unaffected. The physical key is\\n    `<keyPrefix><namespace>:<key>`.\\n\\n## Added\\n\\n- **`keyPrefix`** \u2014 set `false` (or `\'\'`) for the pre-3.0 behaviour, or a string for your own prefix. A\\n  per-adapter `adapters.localStorage.prefix` still wins over it.\\n- **`migrateLegacyKeys`** (default `true`) \u2014 adopt pre-3.0 unprefixed entries on read.\\n\\n## Migration\\n\\n**Most consumers need to do nothing.** On a miss at `strata:<key>`, the adapter looks for the bare `<key>`\\nand, if the value is one of ours, moves it under the prefix and returns it. Your data stays reachable.\\n\\nThree properties of that migration, each verified in a browser:\\n\\n- **It is per key, on read \u2014 never a bulk sweep.** A sweep would adopt every unprefixed envelope on the\\n  origin, including keys belonging to an instance that opted out or to a sibling app still on 2.x.\\n- **It never adopts a value that is not ours** \u2014 the 2.9.0 envelope check is what makes it safe at all.\\n  A planted `_cltk` is left exactly where it is.\\n- **It never overwrites.** A value already at the prefixed key wins and the legacy entry is left alone.\\n\\n\u{1F534} **Take `keyPrefix: false` if anything outside this library reads a physical key directly** \u2014 a\\npre-paint theme script that runs before any module loads, or a logger reading its own level. Those\\nreaders know the exact key name, and a prefix changes it underneath them. Migration keeps the *data*\\nreachable through this library; it cannot fix a hard-coded reader.\\n\\n```typescript\\n// Frozen physical key names, or an external reader \u2014 keep 2.x behaviour:\\nexport const storage = defineStorage({ keyPrefix: false });\\n```\\n\\n\u{1F534} **Two applications sharing one origin, one still on 2.x:** set `migrateLegacyKeys: false` on the\\nupgraded one, so it does not move keys the other still reads. Better, give each app a `namespace` \u2014\\nthey were already colliding before this release.\\n\\n## Fixed\\n\\n- **A live timer no longer keeps a Node process alive.** `setInterval` holds the event loop open, so a\\n  short-lived script \u2014 a build step, a CLI, an SSR warmup \u2014 that created an instance never exited unless\\n  it also called `close()`. Measured: a script doing one `set`/`get` hung until killed at 120s, and now\\n  exits immediately. All three timers (adapter TTL, cross-adapter cleanup, auto-backup) are `unref`\'d;\\n  it is a no-op in browsers.\\n\\nFull history: [the changelog](/reference/changelog). Install: `yarn add strata-storage@3.0.0`."}]}}')}}]);